HTTP Live Streaming (HLS) with AVPlayer
Approach:
Convert incoming audio chunks into an HLS stream (using .m3u8 playlists and .ts/.aac segments) on the server. The iOS AVPlayer natively supports HLS and handles buffering, gapless playback, and adaptive bitrate streaming.

Steps:

Server-Side: Package Coqui TTS audio chunks into HLS segments.

iOS Client: Use AVPlayer to stream the HLS URL.

objc
NSURL *hlsURL = [NSURL URLWithString:@"https://your-server/stream.m3u8"];
AVPlayerItem *playerItem = [AVPlayerItem playerItemWithURL:hlsURL];
AVPlayer *player = [AVPlayer playerWithPlayerItem:playerItem];
[player play];
Pros:

Native support, minimal client-side code.

Automatic gap handling and buffering.
Cons:

Requires HLS server infrastructure.

